{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"new-particular-comet","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Context\nImport help still describes duplicate creation and future batching. ADR 0039 and `cold-stall-chalk` delivered an import-only batching carveout, deferred push, and source-based resumption. The current implementation does not provide whole-file atomicity or automatic repair for every partial import.\n\n## Plan\n- Update canonical import parser help before generated artifacts.\n- Document 256-event chunks for independent create, parent, file-impact or verify-command, and comment passes.\n- State that link and status passes remain per-event.\n- Document deferred push after successful import work.\n- Document serial `source_id` skipping, incomplete-ticket risk after a crash between passes, and concurrent duplicate risk when scans race.\n- Regenerate packaged import help, overview help, and the CLI reference.\n- Correct `docs/import-export.md` without changing importer behavior.\n- Add focused behavioral assertions for generated help and recovery guidance.\n\n## Testing\n- Run `python scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check` to verify packaged and overview help are regenerated from canonical parser help.\n- Run `python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check` to verify the external CLI reference is regenerated from canonical parser help.\n- Run `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_gen_cli_help.py tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py -q` for the focused help-generator and import-documentation contracts.\n- Run `make lint` and `make typecheck` for source checks.\n- Inspect the final diff to confirm that no importer runtime module changed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Canonical import help describes current batching behavior.\n- [x] Canonical import help describes deferred-push behavior.\n- [x] `python scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check` confirms packaged help matches the canonical source.\n- [x] `python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check` confirms the CLI reference matches the canonical source.\n- [x] Overview help carries the canonical import summary.\n- [x] User guidance describes partial results.\n- [x] User guidance describes supported serial rerun behavior.\n- [x] Guidance promises no whole-file atomicity.\n- [x] Guidance promises no automatic completion of partial tickets.\n- [x] Concurrent-import limitations are explicit.\n- [x] Focused help-generator assertions pass under `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_gen_cli_help.py tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py -q`.\n- [x] Focused import-documentation assertions pass under `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_gen_cli_help.py tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py -q`.\n- [x] The final diff contains no importer runtime changes.\n- [x] Import runtime behavior is unchanged.","id":"3b22-52c9-1ca4-431c","parent_id":"e867-0f39-b887-40fa","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"F10 document import batching and partial recovery"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788161026522289001,"uuid":"ba6667bd-105e-443f-a8ea-93eb7f3f9f98"}